Let $a, b, c \in \mathbb{Z}$ and let $|\cdot|$ be as in [[def-int-abs]]. Then

1. $|a| \ge 0$;
2. $|a| = 0$ if and only if $a = 0$;
3. $|-a| = |a|$;
4. $|ab| = |a|\,|b|$;
5. $-|a| \le a \le |a|$;
6. $|a| \le c$ if and only if $-c \le a \le c$.

